<|eom|><|start|>assistant to=user<|message|>In PL/I an array is introduced with a DECLARE statement. The ARRAY attribute
may be written as the keyword ARRAY and the subscript ranges are given in
parentheses after the array name. The data type / storage attributes follow
the dimension specification.

General form

    DCL ARRAY  array-name  ( dimension-spec )  data-attributes

* dimension-spec  =  n  or  low : high  or  dim1 , dim2 , ...
* data-attributes =  FIXED BIN , FIXED DEC , FLOAT , CHAR , etc.

Examples

* One dimensional
    DCL ARRAY SALARY(100) FIXED DEC(7,2);
    DCL ARRAY A(10) FIXED BIN(31);

* Two dimensional
    DCL ARRAY TABLE(5,10) CHAR(20);

* With explicit bounds
    DCL ARRAY C(1:100) FLOAT DEC(53);

The same declaration can also be written in the more usual positional form
DCL name(dim) type, e.g. DCL SALARY(100) FIXED DEC(7,2); which is
syntactically equivalent to the ARRAY keyword form above.

Answer: J
